    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-10-23T17:20:43+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-23T17:20:43+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T06:50:43Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T06:50:43Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough of low pressure that lies near the NT/WA border will combine with a trough and cold front further south to move over much of SA from Saturday, and over the far northeast on Sunday. A ridge of high pressure will then move into the west from late Sunday and persist over the rest of the state throughout next week.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW004" description="Upper South East" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-10-23T15:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T04:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower, most likely later this evening. The chance of a thunderstorm early this evening. Winds west to southwesterly 20 to 25 km/h tending south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the late afternoon.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-10-24T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-23T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the evening. The chance of a thunderstorm in the afternoon and evening. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds, large hail and heavy rain which may lead to flash flooding in the afternoon and evening. Light winds becoming east to southeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the middle of the day then turning southerly 20 to 30 km/h in the early afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the mid to high 20s.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 4:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-25T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-24T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of rain, most likely in the morning and early afternoon. Winds southerly 25 to 35 km/h turning southwesterly in the early afternoon then decreasing to 15 to 25 km/h in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 10 with daytime temperatures reaching around 16.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-26T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-25T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers, most likely in the morning and afternoon. Winds westerly 15 to 25 km/h tending southwesterly during the afternoon then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-10-27T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-10-28T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-26T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-27T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers in the morning and afternoon. Winds northwest to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the day then becoming light during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching around 18.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
